WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.229
Good morning, Hank. It’s Wednesday. I wanna
begin by thanking you for your extraordinarily

00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:07.120
thoughtful and nuanced video about Haiti.
And you also gave us a real way to really

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.240
help, link in the dooblydoo. And I don’t
know how to respond to your brilliance and

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.220
your compassion except by sharing with you
stupid questions that people ask Google.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.030
That’s right, Hank, it’s time for ‘Google
Auto-Fill once again proves that people are

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.030
weird.’

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.730
Hank, today I’m going to answer the top
10 questions people ask Google beginning,

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:22.730
“Why does my…?”

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.449
Why does my eye twitch?
I have great news! Your eye doesn’t twitch.

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:26.449
More on that in a second.

00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:29.340
Why does my cat lick me?
Okay, I’m gonna let you in on a little secret:

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.180
cats believe that all other organisms are
cats. Once you realize that, a lot of cat

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.980
behavior begins to makes sense. So, why does
your cat lick you? Because it thinks it’s

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.160
grooming you. So when your cat licks you he’s
thinking "I love you gigantic hairless cat,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.579
and to show you, I will lick you.”

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:47.380
Why does your urine smell?
Probably because you’re dehydrated, although

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.890
it could be because you have Maple Syrup Urine
Disease. Maple Syrup Urine Disease, which,

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:54.890
by the way, is completely real, is a rare
disease with four main symptoms. The first

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:58.879
is that your urine smells like Maple Syrup.
The other three are coma, brain damage, and

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:01.399
death. But hopefully you just need to drink
some water.

00:01:01.399 --> 00:01:04.899
Why does my dog eat poop?
Because he can. Hank, so a couple of years

00:01:04.899 --> 00:01:09.000
ago I was at the doctor and he said, “You
have a parasite called campylobacter.” And

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.759
I said, “Okay, how do you get that parasite?”
And he said, “You get it from eating feces.”

00:01:13.759 --> 00:01:18.090
And I was like, “Well, I’m just gonna
throw this out there. Umm… just so you know,

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:23.899
I don’t eat feces. I mostly eat, you know,
foods and then that food turns into feces,

00:01:23.899 --> 00:01:27.999
and then I just let the feces go.” And he
was like, “Oh yeah, most people get it by

00:01:27.999 --> 00:01:32.649
being licked by their dogs.” Willy Green,
why did you give me campylobacter?! Anyway,

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:36.679
it turns out dogs eat poop mostly because
they’re bored or stressed out, so if your

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:39.119
dog is eating poop, give him other stuff to
do.

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:42.439
Why does my stomach hurt?
I’d look into the possibility of campylobacter.

00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:46.210
Why does my eyelid twitch?
…Is what you meant earlier when you asked

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:50.959
about your eye twitching. It’s probably
because you stare at screens all day long,

00:01:50.959 --> 00:01:53.619
and googling the problem is not helping.

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:56.439
Why does my cat bite me?
I think that’s what the Zen masters would

00:01:56.439 --> 00:02:00.299
call ‘a question wrongly put.’ The question
isn’t ‘Why does my cat bite me?’ The

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:05.259
question is ‘When did my cat become a vampire,
and what can I do about it?’ And the answers

00:02:05.259 --> 00:02:09.409
are ‘Probably pretty recently or else you’d
already be dead,’ and ‘Nothing. I’m

00:02:09.409 --> 00:02:15.159
sorry. Make your peace with your friends and
with your enemies, because your time is short,

00:02:15.159 --> 00:02:16.489
owner of vampire cat.’

00:02:16.489 --> 00:02:19.840
Why does my stomach growl?
Because your stomach has told your brain to

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.590
tell your stomach that you are hungry, and
that leads to some muscle contractions and

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:26.629
releases of acids and it just blorgoglggog.

00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:30.750
Why does my dog lick everything?
Interestingly, the same reason your dog eats

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.090
poop. It’s because you spend all your time
on the internet and none of your time with

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.680
your dog, so he or she is bored.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:41.140
And lastly, Why does my computer keep freezing?
Why are you being so mean to your computer?

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:44.890
It’s obviously working well enough for you
to Google. But to answer your question, porn-bots.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:48.631
So there you have it, Hank. The ten ‘How
does my…’ questions people ask Google

00:02:48.631 --> 00:02:52.460
the most. I have one for you: How does my
little blue guy fall down every single time

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.460
I make a video?

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.159
Hank, thanks again for reminding us that the
hardest problems are the ones that most need

00:02:56.159 --> 00:02:58.830
solving. I’ll see you on Friday, DFTBA.

